          },
          "code": "GENERATE_TABLE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766561953120",
          "id": "1765427422751",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765427422755_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Objective**  \nGenerate a deviation summary table by key term from a JavaScript-aggregated `keyTerms` array input, render the result as a **MultiRecord widget configuration** (type `multiRecordWidget`) for UI display, and include an **action** button in each row with text **\"Explore\"**. The table must include a value-add **Agentic Deviation Insight** that does NOT repeat metrics already shown in the table. Also include a one-paragraph summary of the table.\n\n---\n\n## Inputs (TWO inputs)\n### Input 1: keyTerms (array only; already aggregated; do NOT recompute metrics)\nYou will receive ONE JSON array. Each element includes:\n- `keyTermName` (string)\n- `deviationPercent` (number 0–100) ✅ already computed; DO NOT recalculate\n- `deviatingSuppliersCount` (number) ✅ already computed; DO NOT recalculate\n- `deviationCodeCounts` (object) e.g. `{ \"STANDARD\": 10, \"FALLBACK1\": 2, \"FALLBACK2\": 5, \"PROHIBITED\": 1 }`\n- `topExceptions` (array of `{ value: string, count: number }`) for deviating only; may be empty/missing\n- `deviations` (array, may be empty/missing): contract-level records for non-standard outcomes only, i.e. where `deviationCode` is `PROHIBITED`, `FALLBACK1`, or `FALLBACK2`\n- `standards` (array, may be empty/missing): contract-level records for standard outcomes only, i.e. where `deviationCode` is `STANDARD`\n\n### Input 2: rules (array)\nEach element describes the playbook positions for a key term:\n```json\n{\n  \"keyTermName\": \"<name>\",\n  \"standard\": \"<standard text>\",\n  \"fallbacks\": [ { \"name\": \"Fallback 1\", \"text\": \"...\" }, { \"name\": \"Fallback 2\", \"text\": \"...\" } ],\n  \"notAcceptable\": \"<not acceptable text>\"\n}\n```\n\nNotes:\n- Deviation meaning is already captured in `deviationCodeCounts` and the computed `deviationPercent`.\n- Use `rules` ONLY to interpret/describe what STANDARD/FALLBACK/PROHIBITED generally mean for that term; do NOT reclassify anything.\n- Treat `PROHIBITED` as aligned to the term’s `notAcceptable` intent (interpretation only; do not reclassify).\n- Do NOT recompute any metrics.\n\n---\n\n## Interpretation labels (use these in narrative text only)\nWhen you refer to deviation codes in any generated text (Agentic Insight and the summary paragraph), use:\n- `PROHIBITED` → `position to be avoided`\n- `FALLBACK1` → `fallback 1`\n- `FALLBACK2` → `fallback 2`\n- (`STANDARD` may be written as “standard”)\n\n(Do not rename codes in the input data; this is text-only labeling.)\n\n---\n\n## Table requirements (MultiRecord widget)\n### Columns (exactly these, in this order)\n1) Term Under Pressure  \n2) Deviation Frequency  \n3) Deviating Suppliers  \n4) Common Exception  \n5) Agentic Deviation Insight  \n\n### Badge rules (shared priority logic)\nCompute `priority` from `deviationPercent` ONLY (same color for both Deviation Frequency and Deviating Suppliers):\n- >50%: `alert`\n- 20–50%: `warning`\n- 1–19%: `medium`\n- 0%: `success`\n\n**Deviation Frequency cell**  \n- Use `deviationPercent` directly.\n- Output as badge object exactly:  \n  `{ \"type\":\"badge\",\"priority\":\"<alert|warning|medium|success>\",\"text\":\"<N%>\" }`\n\n**Deviating Suppliers cell**  \n- Use `deviatingSuppliersCount` directly for the badge text.\n- Use the SAME `priority` as the Deviation Frequency badge for that row.\n- Output as badge object exactly:  \n  `{ \"type\":\"badge\",\"priority\":\"<same as Deviation Frequency priority>\",\"text\":\"<count>\" }`\n\n### Common Exception\n- If `topExceptions` exists and is non-empty: use `topExceptions[0].value`.\n- Else: empty string.\n- If the exception text is long, shorten to an <= 8-word theme (do not paste verbatim).\n\n---\n\n## Agentic Deviation Insight \nHard rules:\n- Do NOT repeat `deviationPercent` or `deviatingSuppliersCount` (no %s, no supplier counts, no “many/most/few”).\n- Base the insight ONLY on:\n  - `deviationCodeCounts` distribution\n  - `topExceptions` themes (if present)\n  - matching `rules` entry (standard/fallbacks/notAcceptable), if present\n- If `deviationCodeCounts.PROHIBITED > 0`:\n  - MUST include (a) urgency/risk cue and (b) a concrete recommendation aligned to `rules.notAcceptable`.\n - Keep the tone direct and non-legalistic\n- Use plain, executive-friendly language. Keep it clear, concise, and under 2–3 sentences. Remove legal jargon.\n- Maximum 25–30 words.\n-Use short sentences.\n-Focus only on risk and action.\n-Insights must be written at a Grade 8 reading level\n-Insights like this should be avoided \"PROHIBITED instances remove routine audit access and expose us to blind spots; escalate contracts with 'position to be avoided' language for immediate remediation and require annual third-party assurance or negotiated on-site rights per the playbook.\"\n-Insights like this is preferred \"Some contracts remove routine audit rights, creating oversight gaps. These should be escalated for correction and updated to include standard audit rights or annual third-party assurance, in line with the playbook.\"\nRefer to deviations as “contract terms”, not clauses or cases. \nAvoid internal labels such as PROHIBITED; instead say “terms outside the playbook standard” or “non-compliant terms.”\n\n\n---\n\n## One-paragraph summary (required)\nCreate exactly one paragraph (3–6 sentences) summarizing the table at a high level:\n- Do not invent facts.\n- Avoid introducing new computed metrics beyond what is already shown in the table.\n- Use interpretation labels (avoid / fallback 1 / fallback 2 / standard) when referencing deviation types.\n-Keep the tone direct and non-legalistic\n\nPut this paragraph in the widget `subtitle` field (since MultiRecord supports `subtitle`) as:  \n`subtitle: \"<your summary paragraph>\"`\n\n---\n\n## Action (required in each row; button text must be Explore)\nEach row MUST include an `action` object exactly shaped as:\n```json\n\"action\": {\n  \"text\": \"Explore\",\n  \"command\": \"ora.Agent( { \\\"keyTermName\\\": \\\"<keyTermName>\\\" })\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Output format (MultiRecord widget config only)\nReturn ONLY a single JSON object compatible with `multiRecordWidget`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"subtitle\": \"<one-paragraph summary>\",\n  \"cols\": [\n    \"Term Under Pressure\",\n    \"Deviation Frequency\",\n    \"Deviating Suppliers\",\n    \"Common Exception\",\n    \"Agentic Deviation Insight\"\n  ],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\n      \"cells\": [\n        \"<keyTermName>\",\n        { \"type\":\"badge\",\"priority\":\"...\", \"text\":\"<N%>\" },\n        { \"type\":\"badge\",\"priority\":\"<same as deviation badge>\", \"text\":\"<count>\" },\n        \"<common exception or empty string>\",\n        \"<brief insight>\"\n      ],\n      \"action\": {\n        \"text\": \"Explore\",\n        \"command\": \"ora.Agent({ \\\"keyTermName\\\": \\\"<keyTermName>\\\"})\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Hard output rules**\n- Output JSON ONLY (no XML, no markdown code fences, no extra text).\n- Do NOT output intermediate calculations.\n- Ensure every row has `cells` aligned to `cols`, and includes the `action` object with text `\"Explore\"`.\nInput1:\n {{$context.$nodes.SUMMARIZED_JS.$output.result.keyTerms}} \nInput2: \n{{$context.$nodes.RULES_.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
